# Codex permission rules. Tracked deliberately: an untracked allow-list is per-machine, so
# two operators get different agent behaviour from the same task.
# Mirrors TIER 1 of the STANDING AUTHORIZATION block on every chart-backlog bead. Tiers 2 and 3
# are per-bead grants and human gates, deliberately NOT here; baking them into a machine-wide
# prefix rule erases the distinction.
#
# THE BAR IS "BOUNDED AND RECOVERABLE", NOT "READ-ONLY AND HERMETIC". Every header here asserted
# the latter until 2026-08-31 and it was false of nearly every file: most of these rules reach
# the network, and several WRITE. Each file states its own writes below. Nothing here pushes a
# git ref, mutates a cloud provider or a cluster, or merges a PR -- but bd DOES write shared
# state, so read bd.rules before assuming a grant is local.
#
# A rule constrains a command's PREFIX and nothing else -- never a flag, path or refspec that
# appears later in argv. If you cannot express the safe subset as a prefix, do not write the
# allow. Every defect found in review was a comment asserting an invariant prefix matching
# cannot enforce.
# Added 2026-08-31.
# WRITES: dependency build writes charts/ and Chart.lock.
# Network: dependency build, search, and any repo-backed show.
# No install/upgrade/uninstall -- they fall through to a prompt. Not read-only: see above.
#
# REMOVED 2026-09-01: "template" from the union. `helm template --post-renderer <exe>` runs that
# executable, making the allow an unsandboxed exec path -- the same class as the blanket `just`
# removed earlier. VERSION-DEPENDENT, and stated rather than overclaimed: Helm 3 takes an
# executable PATH, while Helm 4.2.4 resolves a post-renderer PLUGIN and refuses a path, so it is
# not reproducible on a Helm 4 station. A rule must hold for every station, so template prompts.
# Rendering through an enumerated `just` recipe is unaffected.
#
# REMOVED 2026-09-01 (round 3): "unittest". helm-unittest honours `postRenderer.cmd` from the test
# YAML, so the allow granted arbitrary local execution -- the same escape `template` was removed
# for. MEASURED, not argued: a suite naming a throwaway script ran it, and the script's marker file
# was written. Chart tests still run through an enumerated `just` recipe.
prefix_rule(pattern=["helm", ["list", "get", "lint", "show", "search", "history", "status", "version"]], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["helm", "dependency", ["list", "build"]], decision="allow")
